Nikki's LuCI pages, redesigned around the tasks people come for

The six pages were a plain transcription of the configuration: unlabelled options with no
help text, a Profile page that offered a bare file browser, an editor and log viewer built
from textareas inside a form, and nothing that said whether Nikki was running or set up.
The configuration and its option names are unchanged; only the pages are.

- Every page opens with the same header: what the page is for, a live status (Running,
  Stopped = enabled but not running, Disabled), Restart, and Open Dashboard, which is greyed
  out while the core is down and explains why it cannot open instead of failing silently.
- Overview (was App Config): a three-step "Get started" checklist until a profile exists,
  is chosen and Nikki is enabled; tiles for the profile in use, how traffic is captured,
  the dashboard port and the versions. The procd limits move to an "Advanced: Process"
  card. Every option has a description.
- Profiles: a list of profile files with size, date, an "In use" badge and Use / Edit /
  Download / Delete, plus a drop zone that takes .yaml/.yml only. Subscriptions show a
  usage meter, the expiry with a warning in the last week, a failed last update, and a
  "No URL set" badge on the placeholder subscription the package ships, which can no
  longer be updated or used until it has a real URL. Use applies at once.
- Proxy: tabs named for what they decide (LAN Devices, Router Itself, Bypass), with the
  first-match semantics of the access-control tables spelled out.
- Mixin: says what Unmodified means, splits the DNS tab into DNS and Hosts & Nameservers,
  and explains the options people actually change.
- Editor: a file list grouped by kind, a line under it saying whether edits to that file
  last (the startup profile and subscriptions are regenerated), unsaved-change tracking,
  Ctrl+S, Tab indents, Revert, Download, and ?file= links from the Profiles page.
- Logs: one viewer for the app and core logs with time / level / message columns, level
  colours, a text filter, an errors-only view, follow-the-tail, and download. The debug
  report asks first when Nikki is off, since its script enables and starts it.

Colours, spacing and radii come from the theme (Vantage's --v-* tier, then Bootstrap's
exported tokens), so the pages follow the light/dark switch.

Applies to: https://github.com/nikkinikki-org/OpenWrt-nikki.git @ 0c56ba5f (feeds.conf.default pin).
Upstream status: local to CleanWRT.

